            category: "European pear varieties described for Virginia",
            description: "This variety is sometimes called \"sugar pear.\" The fruit is small and yellowish brown with a pale red russet. The flesh is fine grained, smooth, juicy, and extremely sweet. The tree is fairly resistant to fireblight and is considered to be one of the highest quality pears. It is excellent for canning whole or for making spiced pears."
